From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 23:24:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mtk_eth_soc: sync only the RX buffer of a
 recycled page

The page_pool syncs max_len bytes of every page it recycles for the
device, and max_len was MTK_PP_MAX_BUF_SIZE: 3520 bytes with 4K pages.
The DMA engine writes at most the length given in rxd2, ring->buf_size,
which is 2048 on the MT7986. The Ethernet isn't DMA-coherent there, so
each recycled RX page cleaned 55 cache lines where 32 are written.

Pass the ring's buf_size to mtk_create_page_pool() and use it for
max_len, bounded by MTK_PP_MAX_BUF_SIZE. The window the device writes,
[MTK_PP_HEADROOM, MTK_PP_HEADROOM + buf_size), is cache-line aligned at
both ends here (256 and 2304), so lines the CPU dirtied beyond it (an XDP
tail adjustment, a trailer) never overlap what the device writes.

This is what pesa1234's 999-2725 (MediaTek: RX buffer length 2K ->
1.5K) gains on the page_pool path, where every buffer is a whole page,
without lowering max_mtu to 1518.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c | 11 ++++++++---
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
index f3f82aa..0c3f820 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
@@ -2125,7 +2125,8 @@ static bool mtk_page_pool_enabled(struct mtk_eth *eth)
 
 static struct page_pool *mtk_create_page_pool(struct mtk_eth *eth,
 					      struct xdp_rxq_info *xdp_q,
-					      int id, int size)
+					      int id, int size,
+					      unsigned int buf_size)
 {
 	struct page_pool_params pp_params = {
 		.order = 0,
@@ -2134,7 +2135,11 @@ static struct page_pool *mtk_create_page_pool(struct mtk_eth *eth,
 		.nid = NUMA_NO_NODE,
 		.dev = eth->dma_dev,
 		.offset = MTK_PP_HEADROOM,
-		.max_len = MTK_PP_MAX_BUF_SIZE,
+		/* The DMA engine writes at most the length given in rxd2
+		 * (ring->buf_size), so a recycled page only needs that much
+		 * synced for the device.
+		 */
+		.max_len = min_t(unsigned int, buf_size, MTK_PP_MAX_BUF_SIZE),
 	};
 	struct page_pool *pp;
 	int err;
@@ -3086,7 +3091,7 @@ static int mtk_rx_alloc(struct mtk_eth *eth, int ring_no, int rx_flag)
 		struct page_pool *pp;
 
 		pp = mtk_create_page_pool(eth, &ring->xdp_q, ring_no,
-					  rx_dma_size);
+					  rx_dma_size, ring->buf_size);
 		if (IS_ERR(pp))
 			return PTR_ERR(pp);
 
